  "name": "Question 5",
  "problem": "Consider the following arithmetic sequence:\n\n$$\n{a}_{n+1}={a}_{n}-8,\\,\\,{a}_{1}=2,\\,\\,n\\ge 1\n$$\n\nThe explicit formula for the $n$th term is\n\n${a}_{n}=$\n{{field-1}}$,\\,n\\ge 1.$",
  "worked_solution": "The explicit formula for the $n$th term of an arithmetic sequence is\n\n$$\n{a}_{n}={a}_{1}+(n-1)d,\\,n\\ge 1,\n$$\n\nso we need to determine the first term ${a}_{1}$ and the common difference $d.$\n\nWe are given that the first term is ${a}_{1}=2,$ and we can use the recursive rule to compute the second term, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{2} & ={a}_{1}-8 \\\\  & =2-8 \\\\  & =-6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the first and second terms, we can compute the common difference:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & ={a}_{2}-{a}_{1} \\\\  & =-6-2 \\\\  & =-8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow we substitute ${a}_{1}=2$ and $d=-8$ into the formula for the $n$th term:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}+(n-1)d \\\\  & =2+(n-1)(-8) \\\\  & =2-8n+8 \\\\  & =10-8n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the formula for the $n$th term is\n\n$$\n{a}_{n}=10-8n,\\,n\\ge 1.\n$$",
